        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                "word": "synesthésie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "95baeabd-4f2b-4fe4-803d-387d1d8278b0",
                        "entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "synesthésies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "adad7c16-2851-3c3c-b85b-1144c33ea012",
                        "entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Trouble de la perception des sensations, qui fait éprouver deux perceptions simultanées à la sollicitation d’un seul sens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60b13f25-4a7a-4be7-8b05-7ce06c1f2d36",
                                "sense_id": "adad7c16-2851-3c3c-b85b-1144c33ea012",
                                "text": "Réminiscence des correspondances symbolistes, Sartre convie à d'étranges synesthésies: \"Si je mange un gâteau rose, écrit-il dans lÊtre et le Néant, le goût est en rose; le léger parfum sucré et l'onctuosité de la crème au beurre sont le rose. Ainsi je mange rose comme je vois sucré\"."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b8f721b-4c69-4b2c-85aa-85a6f099525c",
                                "sense_id": "adad7c16-2851-3c3c-b85b-1144c33ea012",
                                "text": "… mais, plus encore, Pierre s'intéressait à la synesthésie qui se manifestait lors des hallucinations : la vivacité psychosensorielle étant censée s'accroître dans la première phase de l'ingestion, il espérait voir des goûts, voir des odeurs et des sons, des sensations tactiles, et que la traduction des sens en images l'aide à comprendre, voire à percer, le mystère de la douleur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aca348e7-a969-43d0-af32-c9d04186462c",
                                "sense_id": "adad7c16-2851-3c3c-b85b-1144c33ea012",
                                "text": "Ambassadeur de sa discipline, il avait découvert sur le tard que sa « mémoire de mammouth » lui venait d’une « anomalie », la synesthésie, ou la capacité innée à associer des éléments sensoriels apparemment sans rapport. Lui pouvait accrocher toute la chronologie de l’Univers sur des milliers de « cordes à linge » mentales et en retrouver le moindre détail à volonté."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "64a2a66f-4a04-4747-b832-67628c07de11",
                                "sense_id": "adad7c16-2851-3c3c-b85b-1144c33ea012",
                                "text": "Atteint de synesthésie depuis toujours, je vois les sons comme autant de couleurs."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac3f6f3f-1b87-372e-87cf-64d944d0b1e1",
                        "entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Métaphore s’appuyant sur la correspondance de plusieurs perceptions sensorielles simultanées."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "468423e7-fa6a-4ba9-94b1-048a4c83ac13",
                                "sense_id": "ac3f6f3f-1b87-372e-87cf-64d944d0b1e1",
                                "text": "Les synesthésies sont le thème de Voyelles, le poème de Rimbaud."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "337c481e-34bc-3c99-9db9-247e3b47cfa3",
                        "entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Coexistence de plusieurs sens dans une œuvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "234579ea-72a2-4968-967d-c4e2530b79b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "target_lang_word": "Synästhesie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Synästhesie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55c8f062-b518-308d-a0b8-80d1a31f3dea",
                                        "entry_id": "50e1a378-e67d-31d7-9006-55d79675f1f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synästhesie ist eine hypersensible Empfindung äußerlicher Sinnesreizung. Synästhetisches Empfinden bedeutet, bei Klängen zum Beispiel zugleich Farben zu sehen oder auf jene Klänge bezogen Geschmack zu empfinden."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6252999-b589-455c-8c97-13b683a5b48b",
                                                "sense_id": "55c8f062-b518-308d-a0b8-80d1a31f3dea",
                                                "text": "Synästhesie kann als vorübergehender Effekt nach der Einnahme von Halluzinogenen auftreten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d93ba8f6-f936-465f-9ed1-97ecce41299a",
                                                "sense_id": "55c8f062-b518-308d-a0b8-80d1a31f3dea",
                                                "text": "„Manche Menschen sehen sogar Farben, wenn sie Klänge hören; die Fachwelt spricht von Synästhesie.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "178f3ca3-f51e-3ac5-88c6-243ba011cd71",
                                        "entry_id": "50e1a378-e67d-31d7-9006-55d79675f1f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "vor allem Verbindung von Sprachlauten mit Farbempfindungen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cd1de42-33df-4c09-a0a5-ef2e5fb34544",
                                                "sense_id": "178f3ca3-f51e-3ac5-88c6-243ba011cd71",
                                                "text": "Recht stabile Synästhesien wurden bei Versuchspersonen entdeckt, denen man Vokale als Reiz gab und die damit bestimmte Farbempfindungen verbanden. Synästhesie tritt auch bei Konsonanten auf, aber wesentlich schwächer und diffuser. Über solche Laut-Farb-Synästhesien berichtet Jakobson."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbd694f9-b4a3-4753-8525-002b2eed071b",
                                                "sense_id": "178f3ca3-f51e-3ac5-88c6-243ba011cd71",
                                                "text": "„Das Thema ist eine Art der Synästhesie, die sogenannte ‚audition colorée‘, bei der die Sinneseindrücke von Farben mit denen der Vokale sprachlich verschmolzen werden sollen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b02cf47-43ec-4e1c-9601-8997968ddfbb",
                                                "sense_id": "178f3ca3-f51e-3ac5-88c6-243ba011cd71",
                                                "text": "„Im Bereich der Onomatopoetica tritt auch die Erscheinung der Synästhesie auf: Wahrnehmungen mit Hilfe anderer Sinnesorgane werden in lautlich-akustische Einheiten umgedeutet: flimmern, schimmern, glitzern, flitzen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9886182-0509-4ff8-9f0c-f21aefbe749d",
                                                "sense_id": "178f3ca3-f51e-3ac5-88c6-243ba011cd71",
                                                "text": "„Das erklärt sich aus einer Erscheinung, die wir Mitempfindungen oder Synästhesien nennen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2579c8f5-4e0e-3e3b-8821-dc37060066d0",
                                        "entry_id": "50e1a378-e67d-31d7-9006-55d79675f1f0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stilmittel, bei dem unterschiedliche Empfindungen durch sprachliche Formulierungen verbunden werden"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Literaturwissenschaft"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "248ae36a-95ef-4490-a667-a3d2f8b7f2a4",
                                                "sense_id": "2579c8f5-4e0e-3e3b-8821-dc37060066d0",
                                                "text": "Als Synästhesie kann man z.B. \"goldener Oktober\" auffassen, wobei eine Zeitangabe mit einer Farbe verschmolzen wird."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8d27a30-02da-4355-86e1-223b289f6f6b",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "target_lang_word": "synesthesia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "synesthesia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a64dcbd-cc6d-30cf-8b15-9db4ee076916",
                                        "entry_id": "a8c3bf6e-30b1-3d7b-a0a8-aeedfceba75d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of synaesthesia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b21e8bcd-bc9e-4f5b-97c4-705208d186ed",
                                                "sense_id": "1a64dcbd-cc6d-30cf-8b15-9db4ee076916",
                                                "text": "[…] R. H. Gault's case of synesthesia in a deaf and blind girl, who could distinguish colors by the sense of smell, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b984018c-f97c-4412-b6d6-1140ba33bb49",
                                                "sense_id": "1a64dcbd-cc6d-30cf-8b15-9db4ee076916",
                                                "text": "Because of this, SSDs are one of the first technologies to meaningfully demonstrate just what synesthesia – or at least one kind of it – might feel like to those who have never had it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b692855d-7b49-4506-9e97-8283f3d7bdd3",
                                                "sense_id": "1a64dcbd-cc6d-30cf-8b15-9db4ee076916",
                                                "text": "[S]ynesthetes themselves can provide the indispensable cues to design a structured qualitative questionnaire: color synesthesias and their variations during sexual arousal, direct physical stimulation, and orgasm […] can help scientists differentiate the specific triggers and their characteristics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a8e681ad-6ebe-4223-93c3-2d7a099c20b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "target_lang_word": "synaesthesia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "synaesthesia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                        "entry_id": "9e4d59d0-0236-3ad4-b078-7cbca2c79513",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A neurological or psychological phenomenon whereby a particular sensory stimulus triggers a second kind of sensation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f0451b1-87b0-4697-afc8-1612d1782515",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "M. [Théodore] Flournoy includes all the phenomena of \"Colored Hearing\" and of \"Mental Forms\" under the convenient and adequate name Synæsthesia—in place of which, to be sure, he himself usually employs the less defensible term Synopsie. […] The phenomena of synæsthesia are divided into three main groups: \"photisms,\" among which are included, as by [Eugen] Bleuler and Lehmann, all the varieties of pseudo-chromesthesia; \"Schemes,\" comprising not only \"forms\" (diagrammes) associated with series of words or numbers, but \"symbols,\" or particular figures associated with single letters, numerals, colors and the like; and \"personifications,\" in which the associated factor is no mere color or form, but has become richer and more concrete."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c98d67ed-c443-4329-9ae9-b8aa4efb2a5f",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "Probably in all of us, though in some men much more distinctly than in others, there exist certain synæsthesiæ or concomitances of sense-impression, which are at any rate not dependent on any recognisable link of association."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16352cc1-f72e-43fa-89eb-8f245efe6a8f",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "[…] R. H. Gault's case of synesthesia in a deaf and blind girl, who could distinguish colors by the sense of smell, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fafdd2c7-fa23-40e6-817a-2402e44c56c2",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "Now just as normal perceptions in terms of sense organs different from those stimulated can be interpreted through common past experiences, so it is likely that synæsthesias may be partly explicable in terms of individual experiences."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8024f7b-63ca-4cb9-aa7d-e586e0f5b6c9",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "Into her darkness, a churning synaesthesia, where her pain was the taste of old iron, scent of melon, wings of a moth brushing her cheek."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "140df732-ecc4-46c3-bdf2-b824c3c80e90",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "For example, I myself have a type of synaesthesia: The sounds of musical instruments will sometimes make me see colors, about a yard in front of me, each color specific and consistent with the particular instrument playing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2174c02-df5a-4c31-a945-bb038283db71",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "Colour is the most commonly induced synaesthetic percept and it can be invoked not only by auditory stimuli, but also by smells, tastes and touch sensations[…]. Other synaesthesiae include musical taste and smell, visual smell, perceptions of shaped or auditory pain, and polymodal synaesthesiae."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f13d4acd-786b-4362-9c22-20a1555b0cd1",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "For me Saturday was a bright red color, just as the other days of the week were chromatically coded. […] This wasn't the true synæsthesia which is such a fascinating mystical hint, a loose thread in the fabric of perception left a-dangle, an unravelling which suggests that we could dissolve all our unreal categories."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c60d37-1099-4d49-b68c-f05421d6069a",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "Synaesthesia can occur particularly powerfully during mescalin and LSD intoxication, and is often given mystical significance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d23397b6-9a2d-4df2-8113-9178252dd657",
                                                "sense_id": "330f84d1-e40f-3e42-a41c-58a7e40ab803",
                                                "text": "[S]ynesthetes themselves can provide the indispensable cues to design a structured qualitative questionnaire: color synesthesias and their variations during sexual arousal, direct physical stimulation, and orgasm […] can help scientists differentiate the specific triggers and their characteristics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f43dbb7-6194-38b4-8bc8-860f351a382a",
                                        "entry_id": "9e4d59d0-0236-3ad4-b078-7cbca2c79513",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The association of one sensory perception with, or description of it in terms of, a different perception that is not experienced at the same time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26f7dc30-b8b3-4975-844c-1e1e15e9b9c7",
                                                "sense_id": "5f43dbb7-6194-38b4-8bc8-860f351a382a",
                                                "text": "On a phonemic level, phenomena of synesthesia have often been described and studied. Practically all children and a good many adults—though for the most part adults will deny it—spontaneously associate sounds, whether phonemes or the timbre of musical instruments, with colors and forms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f653619b-a5c4-40eb-bd5c-8682f773e2dc",
                                                "sense_id": "5f43dbb7-6194-38b4-8bc8-860f351a382a",
                                                "text": "For one of the enigmatic features of synaesthesia is that, within a given cultural group, the kinds of associations made by different subjects occur according to statistically verifiable recurring patterns. As Jakobson explains, ‘when we ask whether /i/ or /u/ is darker, testing such phonic oppositions as grave vs. acute, some of the subjects may respond that this question makes no sense to them, but hardly one will respond that /i/ is the darker of the two’[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47bf5e33-2e51-3569-a619-df1b48548785",
                                        "entry_id": "9e4d59d0-0236-3ad4-b078-7cbca2c79513",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A literary or artistic device whereby one kind of sensation is described in the terms of another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8baabbb5-0f22-4f27-b9b8-b2da27e644f2",
                                                "sense_id": "47bf5e33-2e51-3569-a619-df1b48548785",
                                                "text": "Linking moods with colours is one example of synaesthesia. […] As a tool for improving writing, the idea of synaesthesia is versatile and innovative. Why use only visual references to describe visual impressions? Why just describe sounds using sound-related words? Play with cross-matching the senses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4835e4cd-6701-4a09-9f38-901333affd47",
                                                "sense_id": "47bf5e33-2e51-3569-a619-df1b48548785",
                                                "text": "[I]t may be stated that the concept of synaesthesia is instrumental for understanding music videos, since videos are based on the soundtrack's visual associations. Yet to discuss associations here may cause some problems. […] [Nicholas Cook] seems to be relying on a rather normative conception of synaesthesia, which for its part supports the idea of absolute, nonrepresentational music. The implication of his discussion is that the \"true\" forms of music–image synaesthesia come only in the forms of perception of color or light when hearing a certain musical sound."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67ef98ba-d385-490a-91ed-c1969737c021",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "target_lang_word": "sinestesia",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sinestesia",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e1c13a0-47e2-3834-bb4a-fb674ee832d5",
                                        "entry_id": "e9a91f80-e6c4-3cd1-9e81-59d4a9e1385c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mezcla de varios sentidos diferentes. Un sinestésico puede, por ejemplo, oír colores, ver sonidos, y percibir sensaciones gustativas al tocar un objeto con una textura determinada. No es que lo asocie o tenga la sensación de sentirlo: lo siente realmente. La sinestesia es un efecto común de algunas drogas psicodélicas, como el LSD, la mescalina o algunos hongos tropicales."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Retórica",
                                            "neurología y estilística"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cd78feeb-2167-4715-83d9-058778a4fc62",
                        "source_entry_id": "79ec8c71-4f26-3a9b-a8c9-66b1312a658a",
                        "target_lang_word": "sinestesia",
